  "why_prior_nonsemantic_basis_is_not_sufficient": "The absence of a concrete response, measurable delay or current request does not prove that this definition lacks a conditional temporal obligation. An authored delay is an affirmative temporal relation, just as the restored12027 feature-retention definition has affirmative continuity without a fixed feature. A still image cannot measure a sequence, but a source can declare event timing as narrative context. Treating that limit as proof that all timing meaning is nonsemantic was too strong."
